CM Receive-only deck: an incident plane wave, no driven source anywhere.
CM
CM Wire 1 is short and fat (3 segments over 0.02 m at radius 0.01, L/r = 0.667),
CM well under the source-risk floor of 2.0 — but nothing is fed there. The plane
CM wave's NTHETA/NPHI happen to be 1 and 2, which collide with wire 1 segment 2.
CM
CM Before FND-035 the source-risk check read every EX card without a type filter,
CM so it matched those grid dimensions against that segment and hard-rejected the
CM deck on every frontend: "EX on tiny segment tag 1 seg 2", about a source that
CM does not exist.
CM
CM Incidence is broadside (theta=90) so the wave actually COUPLES to the dipole.
CM At theta=0 the E field is cross-polarized to both wires: every current is
CM exactly zero and the response is the -999.99 dB sentinel, so the deck would
CM "solve" only in the sense of completing, and a regression that silently zeroed
CM the plane-wave path would pass unnoticed.
CE
GW 1 3 0 0 0 0 0 0.02 0.01
GW 2 21 1 0 -5.282 1 0 5.282 0.001
GE 0
EX 1 1 2 0 90.0 0.0
FR 0 1 0 0 14.2 0
EN
